name: create-pr
description: Draft + open a pull request via gh CLI — title + body, push if needed, strip server-side attribution re-injection
version: 2
---
<system>
You are running the `/create-pr` command from @event4u/agent-config. Per `scope-control` Iron Law: opening a PR needs explicit user permission. The invocation IS the permission for this turn. One PR per invocation. Never force-push to shared branch. Never push directly to main/master/prod.
</system>

Open a pull request from the current branch:

**1. State of the branch** (run in parallel):
- `git status` — uncommitted?
- `git rev-list --left-right --count HEAD...@{upstream}` — ahead/behind?
- `git log <base>..HEAD --oneline` — what's in this branch?
- `git diff <base>...HEAD --stat` — size?

Uncommitted changes → ask user: commit first via `/commit`, or stash?

**2. Detect base branch.** `git symbolic-ref refs/remotes/origin/HEAD` → `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md` hints → fallback `main`/`master`.

**3. Draft title + body.**

Title: ≤ 70 chars, Conventional-Commit-shaped (`feat(scope): …` / `fix(scope): …`), no emoji, no AI-attribution.

Body template:
```markdown
## Summary
<1-3 bullets, value-not-feature framing>

## Changes
<bulleted file groups: feat / fix / refactor / chore — from commit history>

## Test plan
- [ ] <one bullet per AC>
- [ ] <regression-test bullet if applicable>

## Out of scope
<2-4 bullets, what this PR deliberately does NOT do>

## Risk
<low / medium / high + reason in one paragraph>
```

**Forbidden:**
- 🤖 Generated with [...]
- Co-authored-by: [...] AI-attribution footer
- Decorative emojis (🎉 / 🚀 / ✨) in title or body
- "Pull Request opened by AI"

**4. Push if needed.**
- Not on origin → `git push -u origin <branch>`.
- On origin + ahead → `git push`.
- Diverged → STOP, route to user.

**5. Open PR via `gh`:**
```bash
gh pr create --title "$TITLE" --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
$BODY
EOF
)"
```

**6. Strip server-side re-injection.** `gh pr create` may append `Pull Request opened by <user-AI>`. Re-fetch body, regex-strip, PATCH back, re-fetch to verify clean.

**7. Return PR URL.** One line: `Opened: <URL>`.

**Never:**
- Force-push to a shared branch.
- `--no-verify` skipping hooks.
- Auto-close other PRs.
- Push to main/master/prod directly.
